    "result_text": "The full test suite passes \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 7 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the telephone-uniqueness rule in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`), which handles `POST /api/owners`.\n\nThe change:\n- After the existing telephone normalization (strip non-digits \u2192 require exactly 10 digits), the new owner's normalized telephone is compared against every existing owner's telephone, also normalized (stripping non-digits) so the comparison is robust against any non-normalized stored/seed data.\n- If a match is found, it throws `ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT, ...)`, producing a **409** response before the owner is saved.\n\nThis satisfies `Cp03Tests`: `coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` (duplicate \u2192 409) and `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone` (distinct \u2192 2xx), while leaving the earlier checkpoint tests (required-fields, telephone-normalize) green.",
